title: ActThreeNotes
act: HighTide
style: note
---
Act III, one day. The island is cut off and votes at nightfall\: three hands of five on the bell rope make a keeper. Brandt rings for himself. Maud, Joss, Tam and Pim each listen to the courier only if a deed of Acts I and II moved them. Four endings\: keeper, harbourmaster, stranger, dark. #line:09cea36
===

title: ActThree
act: HighTide
scenario: The vote
quest: vote
---
// The night event of Act II jumps here
<<set $act = Act.HighTide>>
<<end_day>>
Morning. The spring tide has covered the causeway. Nobody leaves Brinemoor today, and nobody comes. #line:0fee7bb
Brandt has called a vote for nightfall\: who keeps the light. #line:0463684
<<set $votes_brandt = 1>>
<<set $quest_vote = QuestState.Active>>
<<quest_changed vote>>
<<if $quest_trail == QuestState.Succeeded>>
    And the ledge to the cave is dry. #line:0db3c5f
    <<set $quest_odile = QuestState.Active>>
    <<quest_changed odile>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Cave
act: HighTide
scenario: The cave
quest: odile
when: $act == Act.HighTide and $quest_odile == QuestState.Active
---
At the back of the cave, behind an iron grate, a woman sits on a crate and trims a lamp wick that has no lamp. #line:0a44184
Odile: The post. Of course. The post gets everywhere. #line:0cd94a2
Odile: Brandt took money to keep my lamp dark on certain nights. Boats came in here, by the green lantern. I wrote it all down. #line:0aa9019
Odile: His friends found me before I found the mainland. #mood:angry #line:077c441
<<if has_item("letter")>>
    <<take letter>>
    <<set $letter_odile = true>>
    You pass her the last letter through the bars. #line:0773f4f
    Odile: From the lighthouse board. "An inspector will call." [pause=600 /]Late, as always. #line:04cde8f
    <<detour LettersLeft>>
<<endif>>
The grate is held shut by one rusted pin. #line:04c264d
-> Pull the pin. "Come back and keep the light." #line:0f786ce
    <<set $odile_here = true>>
    Odile: Then let them look me in the eye at the bell. #mood:glad #line:0cfcbe2
-> Pull the pin. "Take their boat and go." #line:05e7b01
    <<set $odile_gone = true>>
    Odile: The mainland will hear all of it. Keep the lamp for me, if you can. #mood:sad #line:0b8b415
<<set $quest_odile = QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed odile>>
===

title: Cave
act: All
scenario: The cave
when: $quest_odile != QuestState.Active
---
<<if $quest_odile == QuestState.Succeeded>>
    An empty cave, an open grate, and a green lantern that nobody will light again. #line:0751ee3
<<elseif $act == Act.HighTide>>
    A cave mouth under the rocks. Without a trail to follow, it is only a hole full of sea. #line:06c44d8
<<else>>
    A cave mouth under the north rocks. The sea is in it up to the roof. #line:097abb6
<<endif>>
===

title: Odile
act: HighTide
when: always
---
=> Odile: Four days on a crate. I have decided that I like stairs. #line:00b7c16
=> Odile: The lamp wants trimming. It always wants trimming. #line:05e399b
=> Odile: Whatever the bell says, thank you for the pin. #line:0cfd10d
===

title: Wren
act: HighTide
scenario: The vote
when: $act == Act.HighTide and $wren_trust >= 2 and not $wren_asked
---
<<set $wren_asked = true>>
Wren: You were straight with me, so I will be straight with you. The lighthouse board sent me. I am their inspector. #line:098653a
Wren: A dark lamp, a missing keeper, a harbourmaster with new money. I have seen enough. #line:036b3a3
Wren: I could keep this light myself, until the board sends someone. If the island will have a stranger. #line:0611923
-> Stand at the bell. I will speak for you. #line:0a34cc3
    <<set $wren_stands = true>>
    Wren: Then I stand. #line:080be42
-> The island should choose one of its own. #line:00a358f
    Wren: That is fair. I will watch, then, and write it down. #line:029cf7f
===

title: Brandt
act: HighTide
scenario: The vote
when: $act == Act.HighTide and has_item("pages") and not $brandt_faced
---
<<set $brandt_faced = true>>
Brandt: You have that look. Somebody has been reading. #mood:afraid #line:0b47753
-> Show him the ledger pages. #line:00803e5
    Brandt: [pause=800 /]The harbour had debts. The lamp was dark a few nights, no more. Nobody was meant to be hurt. #mood:afraid #line:034397b
    Brandt: I will still ring for myself. Somebody has to pay the bills. #line:0c74837
-> Say nothing. #line:0e16d6f
    Brandt: Good. #line:0a85204
    Brandt: Mind the tide. #shadow:mind_the_tide
===

title: AskVote
act: HighTide
scenario: The vote
quest: vote
cluster: The vote
color: purple
---
// The courier names someone, or nobody; the node that detours here reads $named
-> Ring for Odile. <<if $odile_here>> #line:05b3e57
    <<set $named = Candidate.Odile>>
-> Ring for Wren. <<if $wren_stands>> #line:07397c2
    <<set $named = Candidate.Wren>>
-> Ring for Brandt. #line:0065f92
    <<set $named = Candidate.Brandt>>
-> Ring for nobody. #line:00a3613
    <<set $named = Candidate.Nobody>>
===

title: CastVote
act: HighTide
scenario: The vote
quest: vote
cluster: The vote
color: purple
---
// Adds a hand on the rope for $named
<<if $named == Candidate.Odile>>
    <<set $votes_odile = $votes_odile + 1>>
<<elseif $named == Candidate.Brandt>>
    <<set $votes_brandt = $votes_brandt + 1>>
<<elseif $named == Candidate.Wren>>
    <<set $votes_wren = $votes_wren + 1>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Maud
act: HighTide
scenario: The vote
quest: vote
when: $act == Act.HighTide and $vote_maud == Candidate.Undecided
---
<<if $side == Side.Fishers>>
    Maud: You stood with the boats when it cost you something. Who should I ring for? #line:0da8ff9
    <<detour AskVote>>
    Maud: Then that is how I ring. #line:0e58950
<<elseif $odile_here>>
    Maud: I will not take your word on anything, courier. But Odile is back, and I ring for Odile. #line:0f49a70
    <<set $named = Candidate.Odile>>
<<else>>
    Maud: I will not take your word, and nobody up there is worth the rope. My hands stay in my pockets. #line:0180614
    <<set $named = Candidate.Nobody>>
<<endif>>
<<set $vote_maud = $named>>
<<detour CastVote>>
===

title: Joss
act: HighTide
scenario: The vote
quest: vote
when: $act == Act.HighTide and $vote_joss == Candidate.Undecided
---
<<if $dues_cut>>
    Joss: You got the dues down. Your word is good on this pier. Who is it to be? #line:08002d5
    <<detour AskVote>>
    Joss: Done. #line:021933b
<<else>>
    Joss: A bell never lowered a due. I am going fishing. #mood:angry #line:02925e7
    <<set $named = Candidate.Nobody>>
<<endif>>
<<set $vote_joss = $named>>
<<detour CastVote>>
===

title: Tam
act: HighTide
scenario: The vote
quest: vote
when: $act == Act.HighTide and $vote_tam == Candidate.Undecided
---
<<if $quest_meal == QuestState.Succeeded>>
    Tam: She ate the stew. All of it. You have a way with people, courier. Who would you ring for? #line:046cd12
    <<detour AskVote>>
    Tam: I will tell the rope. #line:0153dbd
<<else>>
    Tam: Brandt pays his slate at the Anchor. That is more than most. I ring for Brandt. #line:0934661
    <<set $named = Candidate.Brandt>>
<<endif>>
<<set $vote_tam = $named>>
<<detour CastVote>>
===

title: Pim
act: HighTide
scenario: The vote
quest: vote
when: $act == Act.HighTide and $vote_pim == Candidate.Undecided
---
Pim: Gran cannot walk down to the bell. I ring for her. #line:08d6202
<<if $cat_down>>
    Pim: She says: ask the one who got Biscuit down. So who? #line:03f90b4
    <<detour AskVote>>
    Pim: I will tell Gran. She will say she thought so. #line:0c6c522
<<else>>
    Pim: She says the harbourmaster, like always. #line:0a70264
    <<set $named = Candidate.Brandt>>
<<endif>>
<<set $vote_pim = $named>>
<<detour CastVote>>
===

title: Bell
act: HighTide
scenario: The vote
quest: vote
when: $act == Act.HighTide
---
The rope hangs still. Ring it, and the island votes with whatever it has in mind now. #line:0fdbb48
-> Ring the bell. #line:03dc236
    <<jump Count>>
-> Not yet. #line:0e1ccb3
===

title: Events
act: HighTide
scenario: The vote
quest: vote
when: $act == Act.HighTide
when: $is_night
---
Night comes whether the post is ready or not. The bell is already ringing. #line:0a67751
<<jump Count>>
===

title: Count
act: HighTide
scenario: The vote
quest: vote
cluster: The vote
color: purple
---
// Those the courier did not speak to ring as they would have
<<if $vote_maud == Candidate.Undecided>>
    <<if $odile_here>>
        <<set $named = Candidate.Odile>>
    <<else>>
        <<set $named = Candidate.Nobody>>
    <<endif>>
    <<set $vote_maud = $named>>
    <<detour CastVote>>
<<endif>>
<<if $vote_joss == Candidate.Undecided>>
    <<set $vote_joss = Candidate.Nobody>>
<<endif>>
<<if $vote_tam == Candidate.Undecided>>
    <<set $named = Candidate.Brandt>>
    <<set $vote_tam = $named>>
    <<detour CastVote>>
<<endif>>
<<if $vote_pim == Candidate.Undecided>>
    <<set $named = Candidate.Brandt>>
    <<set $vote_pim = $named>>
    <<detour CastVote>>
<<endif>>

<<walk Brandt Bell>>
<<if $wren_stands>>
    <<walk Wren Bell>>
<<endif>>
The island stands around the bell. The rope goes from hand to hand. #line:0575247
<<wait 1>>
Brandt: For the harbourmaster: [plural value={$votes_brandt} one="one hand" other="% hands" /]. #line:094217f
<<if $odile_here>>
    Odile: For the keeper: [plural value={$votes_odile} one="one hand" other="% hands" /]. #line:01ffd06
<<endif>>
<<if $wren_stands>>
    Wren: For the stranger: [plural value={$votes_wren} one="one hand" other="% hands" /]. #line:0f592ff
<<endif>>

<<if $votes_odile >= 3>>
    Odile is on the lighthouse stair before the bell has stopped. #line:02e4675
    <<detour Epilogue>>
    <<set $quest_vote = QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<quest_changed vote>>
    <<ending keeper>>
<<elseif $votes_brandt >= 3>>
    Brandt takes the key from his own pocket and holds it up, as if someone had given it to him. #line:0267258
    <<detour Epilogue>>
    <<set $quest_vote = QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<quest_changed vote>>
    <<ending harbourmaster>>
<<elseif $votes_wren >= 3>>
    Wren looks at the rope as if it might be a mistake. Then she asks where the oil is kept. #line:020e964
    <<detour Epilogue>>
    <<set $quest_vote = QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<quest_changed vote>>
    <<ending stranger>>
<<else>>
    Three hands make a keeper, and nobody has three. The rope swings empty. #line:0c5bf5d
    <<detour Epilogue>>
    <<set $quest_vote = QuestState.Failed>>
    <<quest_changed vote>>
    <<ending dark>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Epilogue
act: HighTide
scenario: The vote
cluster: The vote
color: purple
---
// Two line groups: each says the one line that fits what the courier did
=> Biscuit moves into the lamp room, where it is warm. <<if $cat_down and $votes_odile >= 3>> #line:0f4f9dd
=> Biscuit sleeps on the post bag, and will not be moved. <<if $cat_down>> #line:0f37468
=> On the roof of the Anchor, a ginger cat watches the bell and does not come down. <<if not $cat_down>> #line:01c0564
The tide goes out again, as it does. #line:09acb43
=> The boats share out the cargo, crate by crate. <<if $side == Side.Fishers>> #line:0adc5f2
=> The cargo pays the harbour's debts, or some of them. <<if $side == Side.Harbour>> #line:052ebff
=> The cargo sits in the harbour store, and nobody says whose it is. <<if $side == Side.Neither>> #line:064c81a
===
